  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R24", "R10"],
      "pins": ["J2.3", "J5.3"],
      "nets": ["NET0038", "NET0015", "NET0013"],
      "observed": "In the servo-signal block on the right of the sheet, the resistors that sit in series between the PWM source nets (NET0038 for channel 1, NET0015 for channel 2) and the servo-header signal pins (J2 pin 3, J5 pin 3) are drawn as 0 Ω (R24 and R10). There is no 1 kΩ resistor anywhere on the schematic; every resistor in that block reads 0 Ω.",
      "expected": "The specification states that the PWM signal lines carry 1 kΩ series resistors: 'R3, R4 | 1k each | Series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3 respectively.' Only the serial-mode bridge jumpers (R13/R14) are meant to be 0 Ω; the series position must be 1 kΩ.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R3, R4 | 1k each | Series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3 respectively."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Right-side servo block: NET0038 -[R24 0]- J2 pin3 and NET0015 -[R10 0]- J5 pin3; the only resistor values present on the sheet are 0, 2k, 2.2k, 5.1k, 10k, 20k, 47k — no 1k."}
      ],
      "impact": "The intended 1 kΩ series current-limiting / protection on each PWM servo signal line is absent; the M5Stack GPIO drives the servo input directly. This deviates from the documented PWM signal conditioning and removes the series protection the reference design provides.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build is otherwise a faithful (renumbered) implementation of the spec — power paths, diode orientations, bulk/decoupling caps, the MAX3485 self-switching direction circuit and the 0 Ω PWM-select/serial-bridge jumpers all match — but the two 1 kΩ series resistors the spec mandates on the PWM servo lines (R3/R4) are populated as 0 Ω, which is the one deviation the drawing supports."
}

